  "term": "codification",
  "definition": "Codification is the process of organizing law into a formal code that aims to state a whole area of rights, remedies, or penalties in written form. In this historical usage, it is contrasted with mere compilations or revisions of statutes, which replace earlier laws without fully covering the field.",
